{"context":"Steward must orchestrate existing AI coding-agent CLIs. ACP (Agent Client Protocol) is the candidate bridge; it has protocol versions and requires the client to handle `session/request_permission` and structured context. Claude Code and Codex do not speak ACP natively.","decision":"Pin ACP v1. Driver config is `{tool, cmd, args}`. Provide adapters for Claude Code and Codex (they need adapters; opencode speaks ACP). The steward client MUST answer `session/request_permission` with a default-deny policy engine and must never hang. The structured-context and permission-callback questions are resolved by the acp-client-spike before build.","consequences":"A single pinned protocol keeps the bridge stable; adapters isolate non-ACP CLIs. Default-deny is safe by default but may block legitimate prompts until the policy is configured. Cost: adapters and a policy engine to maintain; the v1 pin means a future ACP v2 is a deliberate upgrade.","alternativesConsidered":"ACP v2 (rejected for v1: less settled, probe deferred). Ad-hoc per-tool protocols (rejected: N integrations, no shared permission model). A bespoke protocol (rejected: reinvents ACP).","appliesTo":["eka-steward/**"]}